<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis Q1 sales up 22 pct.</title>
<headline>Novartis Q1 sales up 22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p>Group Sales by division</p>
<p>    Healthcare		  4,499	    vs 3,549</p>
<p> Pharmaceuticals		3,389	    vs 2,605</p>
<p> Consumer Health		421		vs 383</p>
<p> Generics			 362		vs 295</p>
<p> Ciba Vision		    327		vs 266</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>    Agribusiness		2,713	    vs 2,314</p>
<p> Crop protection		1,806	    vs 1,512</p>
<p> Seeds			    685		vs 560</p>
<p> Animal Health		  222		vs 242</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>    Nutrition		   964		vs 820</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>    Total			 8,176	    vs 6,683</p>
<p>Note - Full name of Swiss pharmaceuticals and life sciences group is Novartis AG. The company's sales were 22 percent higher on a Swiss franc basis and eight percent higher in local currencies.  </p>
<p>Quarterly data for 1996 period redefined for comparison purposes and do not include divested business activities.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
